{"B_expression":"-1/(2*(1+u)*((1+u)+sqrt((1+u)**2+r))**2)","C_expression":"-1/(2*(1+u))","derivation":"Retain the inherited exact-root coefficient pair. The algebraic identity is verified: with a=1+u and s=sqrt(a^2+r), the exact correction is g_exact=r/(a+s). Decomposing r/(a+s)=r/2+r^2*B+u*r*C gives the constraint r*B+u*C=1/(a+s)-1/2. Substituting B=-1/(2a(a+s)^2) and C=-1/(2a) and using a=1+u (so 1-a=-u) the numerator simplifies to -a(2u(a+s)+r), dividing to -(2u(a+s)+r)/(2(a+s)^2)=(1-u-s)/(2(a+s)), confirming the identity. On the closed outer rectangle |r|<=1/2, |u|<=1/4: a>=3/4>0 and a^2+r>=9/16-1/2=1/16>0, so sqrt is analytic on an open neighborhood. Generation-1 feedback (now inherited as active state) confirms all in-support rows achieve residuals at machine epsilon (~1e-71), while out-of-support rows (|u|>1/4 or |r|>1/2) correctly fall to the linear g=r/2 fallback via chi gating. No numerical evidence of failure motivates revision.","inspect":[{"file_id":"CALC/draft.json","limit":4096,"offset":0}],"note":"Successor: retain this program for subsequent stages. Key invariants: (1) a=1+u>=3/4 and a^2+r>=1/16 on the outer rectangle, so the sqrt is analytic with no branch cut. (2) The C term -1/(2a) is essential for u!=0: it absorbs the 2*u*g cross contribution in the whole residual E=(2g+g^2-r)+2*u*g. (3) Outside chi support (|r|>1/4 or |u|>1/8) the host applies g=r/2; large-deviation rows (z far from 1) are by design outside support and are not program failures. (4) Each stage must consume the actual stored z, not an ideal root. (5) The analytic certificate is ANALYTIC_ON_CORE_NEIGHBORHOOD / CONDITIONAL_SMOOTH_FAMILY; this is a source-relative coefficient family only, not a full PDE certificate. (6) The weighted column residuals at in-support points are at or below ~1e-84, confirming the algebraic cancellation is numerically realized."}